caddy-tui (1.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New [h] screen: HTTPS certificates. Lists the certificates Caddy has
    stored (names, issuer, expiry) and warns when one is about to expire, when
    a domain has none yet, or when Let's Encrypt/ACME is failing for it.
  * The diagnostics also report certificate problems.

 -- Miguel González Oreiro <mgoreiro@gmail.com>  Sat, 17 Oct 2026 22:00:00 +0200

caddy-tui (1.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Interface translated: English (default) and Spanish, chosen at startup
    from --lang, CADDY_TUI_LANG, a saved preference ([L] key) or the system
    locale.
  * Packaged as a Debian package (architecture-independent).
  * Fix: snippets such as "(name) {" were counted as sites.

 -- Miguel González Oreiro <mgoreiro@gmail.com>  Sat, 17 Oct 2026 21:00:00 +0200
